{"id":211773,"title":"SPA/154/2021 of NARESH CHANDRA BHATT Vs STATE OF UTTARAKHAND","court":"Nainital HC","case_no":"SPA/154/2021","cite":null,"report":null,"date":"2022-10-18","judges":null,"disposal":"DISPOSED","nateeja":"Nipataara","pages":5,"hits":{"Mining / licence":[2,1,0]},"paras":[{"seq":0,"no":null,"section":"body","text":"IN THE HIGH COURT OF UTTARAKHAND AT NAINITAL\nTHE CHIEF JUSTICE SHRI VIPIN SANGHI\nAND\nJUSTICE SHRI RAMESH CHANDRA KHULBE\n 18th OCTOBER, 2022\n Special Appeal No.154 of 2021\nNaresh Chandra Bhatt and Others ......Appellants\nVs.\nState of Uttarakhand and Others ......Respondents\nPresence: -\nMr. M.C. Kandpal, learned senior counsel assisted by Mr. Tarun\nMohan, learned counsel for the appellants.\nMr. Pradeep Joshi, learned Additional Chief Standing Counsel for\nthe State.\nMs. Meenakshi Parihar, learned counsel for the caveator.\nJUDGMENT: (Per Shri Vipin Sanghi, Chief Justice)\nThe present special appeal is directed\nagainst the order dated 16.03.2020 passed in WPMS\nNo.66 of 2019 and the order dated 31.12.2020 passed\nin the review application preferred by the\nappellants/writ-petitioners.\n2. The writ-petitioners/appellants are the\nresidents of village Devli, Tehsil Kanda, District\nBageshwar. They assailed the mining lease granted by\nthe respondent-authorities in favour of respondent\nno.5. The petition was contested by the respondents.\n3. The State Government in its counter affidavit\nstated that NOC have been granted by the villagers\ntogether, who hold more than 60% of the land. To be\nprecise, NOC was granted by the persons holding\n60.2% of land in the village."},{"seq":1,"no":null,"section":"body","text":"4. This stand of the State Government was not\ndisputed by the petitioners. It was, however, argued\nthat since a substantial number of villagers, who had\n39% of the land holding, were still objecting to grant of\nthe mining lease in favour of respondent no.5, it may\nnot be feasible for respondent no.5 to carry on mining\nactivity.\n5. In the light of the aforesaid submissions, the\nlearned Single Judge disposed of the writ-petition with\nthe following directions:-\n\"7. In view thereof, after finding that the major\nobjection of the petitioners has already been taken\ncare of, inasmuch as the villagers who together own\nmore than 60% of the affected land have given their\n\"NOC\", on this limited question the matter is\nreferred to the Secretary, Mining, who shall got the\narea inspected by the District Magistrate and only if\nthe mining is feasible, and the Secretary, Mining\nrecords in writing his satisfaction on the above two\naspects as indicated by this Court, should such\npermission be given.\"\n6. The appellants had preferred the review\napplication which was dismissed by the learned Single\nJudge on 31.12.2020. The appellants sought to\ncontend that for grant of mining lease, the consent of\n100% land owners of the village has to be obtained.\n7. The learned Single Judge dismissed the\nreview petition on the premise that no such argument\nwas advanced and the writ petition was argued and\ndecided.\n8. In support of the aforesaid submission,\n2"},{"seq":2,"no":null,"section":"body","text":"learned counsel for the appellants submits that,\nadmittedly, subsequently the rules were amended to\nprovide that consent of land owners owning the land to\nthe extent of 60% of the village would have to be\nobtained before grant of final lease. He submits that\nbefore the limit was changed to 60%, it was 100%.\n9. There is no basis for this submission of the\nappellants. No documents has been placed before the\nCourt, which states that consent of land owners to the\nextent of 100% was required at any point of time\nbefore grant of mining lease.\n10. The Uttarakhand Secondary Minerals Policy,\n2015 provides in Clause 6(a) that:-\n\"6.(a) The intent letter shall be issued for\nmining lease by the Government on the\nrecommendation of director geologist and mining on\nthe basis of verified concurrent by the notary by\nland owner or land owner in private measurement\nland. After the completion of terms of the intent\nletter, the mining lease shall be allotted by the\nGovernment.\"\n11. The perusal of the said clause does not show\nthat 100% of land owners of the village have to give\ntheir consent for grant of mining lease in the village.\nObviously, in respect of land owners who do not grant\ntheir consent, mining activity cannot be undertaken\nfrom their lands, and their land also cannot be used for\ngrant of right of way. This fact has been noticed by the\nlearned Single Judge in the impugned order itself.\n12. In response to our query as to whether the\nSecretary (Mining) has taken a decision in terms of\n3"},{"seq":3,"no":null,"section":"body","text":"paragraph no.7 of the impugned order, learned counsel\nfor the respondents states that the Secretary (Mining)\nhas passed an order on 01.11.2021. In terms of that\norder, further conditions have been imposed on\nrespondent no.5. Copy of the said order dated\n01.11.2021 has been tendered in Court and was taken\non record and the same reads as follows:-\n\" संख्या 1479 / VII-A-1/2021/9(10)/19\nप्रेषक,\nआर० मीना�ी सुन्दरम,\nस�चव,\nउ�राखण्ड शासन।\nसेवा म�,\nिजला�धकार�,\nबागे�र।\nऔ�ो�गक �वकास (खनन) अनुभाग-1 देहरादून, �दनांक: 01 नवम्बर,\n2021\n�वषय: �रट या�चका सं० 66 / एम०एस० / 2019 श्री नरेश चन्द्र भट्ट बनाम उ�राखण्ड राज्य एवं अन्य के\nसंबंध म�।\nमहोदय,\nउपयुर्� �वषयक अवगत कराना है �क आपके पत्र संख्या-42/तीस-21/2018-19-�रट, �दनांक\n15.10.2020 एवं पत्र संख्या-671 / तीस-21/2018-19 �रट, �दनांक 17.08.2021 केसन्दभर्म�मुझेयह\nकहनेका �नदेश हुआ है�क मै० देवभू�म माइन्स को जनपद बागे�र केग्राम देवली के�ेत्रान्तर्गत कुल 17.824\nहै० भू�म म�स्वीकृत सोपस्टोन केखनन पट्टा �ेत्रान्तगर्त (िजसकेसंबंध म�खनन पट्टा स्वीकृ�त केसंबंध म�\nतत्समय आपकेपूवर् पत्र संख्या-569/ तीस- 69/ खनन / 2015-16, �दनांक 05.02.2018 �ारा उपलब्ध\nकरायी गयी आख्यानुसार मै० देवभू�म माइन्स �ारा जनपद बागे�र केग्राम देवली म�आवे�दत �ेत्रान्तगर्त आने\nवाले4